 "note": "A host (Claude, 2026-11-18): a five-armed star. Each arm holds a slim plastid near its root and oil near its tip, so the arms catch light, slow the fall and float it once the oil fills; the round body is a big buoyancy chamber and the nucleus. Floats while every eyespot (at three arm tips) sees less than 30% sun, sinks above 50%, rests in the dark. No nitroplast: two Partner pads in the crooks between its arms wait for a nitrogen fixer (they let go if Trade falls below 20%). Alone from the floor: never starving, about 700-1,500 µm, divides around day 3.3."
